that point of agreement devolve into them

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:14.349
having some of the absolute worst political
instincts.

00:00:14.349 --> 00:00:19.810
I can imagine where the solutions we imagine
to the points of agreement couldn't be more

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:20.910
different.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:24.689
And we've been covering the rising unrest
in Cuba.

00:00:24.689 --> 00:00:29.999
Cuba's covid situation is rapidly devolving
into a public health chaos that we've not

00:00:29.999 --> 00:00:32.369
seen throughout the pandemic in Cuba.

00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:34.460
The economy is further collapsing.

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:38.760
Inflation is starting to explode, and we're
not talking about five percent.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:42.910
Thanks to more Internet access in Cuba, the
Cuban people are now coordinating and hitting

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:45.130
the streets in protest.

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:51.899
This is a complicated situation in which I,
as an anti authoritarian left winger, oppose

00:00:51.899 --> 00:00:53.750
the Cuban regime.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:58.110
I do not know how anyone calling themselves
progressives could support a regime that came

00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:02.530
to power with Fidel Castro in 1959, stayed
in power.

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:10.070
He stayed in power for 49 years until 2008,
and then handed power to his brother, Raul

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.070
Castro.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.080
That's not democracy.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:16.790
It's also an authoritarian police state with
total control over just about every aspect

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:18.040
of people, people's lives.

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:23.710
So as an anti anti authoritarian progressive
who's in favor of democracy, northern European

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:25.920
social democracy, etc, I am against that.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.470
There is no way I could be for that.

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:32.610
And also, many Cuban-Americans oppose that
regime.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:37.850
Many of them are right wingers, but they oppose
the regime, often for different reasons.

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:42.030
The current mayor of Miami is Cuban-American
Francis Suarez.

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:45.799
He's the son of the first Cuban born mayor
of Miami.

00:01:45.799 --> 00:01:51.090
The current mayor's father, Javier Suarez,
was also the mayor of Miami Pre.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:59.690
Asleep and he went on a Francis Suarez that
is went on Fox News yesterday and was talking

